# Data — raw CSVs are downloaded by scripts/download_data.py, never committed
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/processed/
# NOTE: data/dashboard/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Those slim tables are
# committed so the Streamlit Cloud deploy has data on a cold start without
# re-downloading 126 MB of raw CSVs. Regenerate with:
#   python scripts/export_dashboard_data.py

# Model artifacts.
#
# clv_model.joblib IS committed (129 KB) and must stay committed: the
# dashboard's model-comparison tab, ROI section and what-if scorer all load it,
# and Streamlit Cloud has no way to run training on a cold boot. Ignoring it
# silently degraded three sections of the deployed app.
# Anything larger than a few MB should be pulled from a release instead.
artifacts/*.pkl
!artifacts/clv_model.joblib

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
